{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden-render regression cases for mw909 (tests/golden/CMakeLists.txt registers one CTest per case,",
    "label 'golden'). Each case is a command line for tools/mw909-render; the harness appends --quiet --out.",
    "  id        : unique, [a-z0-9_]+; the blessed render is blessed/<id>.wav",
    "  args      : mw909-render arguments; @GOLDEN_DIR@ expands to this directory",
    "  reference : optional id of another case whose blessed file this render must match (no file of its own)",
    "  tol       : optional mw909-wavcompare tolerance (absolute, or lsb:<n>); default one LSB of the file",
    "  note      : what the case covers",
    "Voice cases use the tool's stock machine; pattern cases use --kit stock (or --mix typical, the tool's own",
    "mix) except where a factory kit or preset is the point. Factory memories are used by index or name, so a",
    "change to the factory library is a sound change that needs a re-bless. A case whose blessed file does not",
    "exist yet is reported as SKIPPED, never as passed.",
    "Re-bless after an intended sound change: BLESS_REASON='why' tools/bless_goldens.sh <build-dir>"
  ],
